Implemented Vercel Speed Insights for SheetSnap Desktop

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights following the official documentation (https://vercel.com/docs/speed-insights/quickstart).

## Changes Made:

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/speed-insights` version 2.0.0 via npm
- Updated package.json and package-lock.json with the new dependency

### 2. Code Integration
- Modified `app/layout.tsx` to integrate Speed Insights:
  - Added import: `import { SpeedInsights } from "@vercel/speed-insights/next";`
  - Added `<SpeedInsights />` component at the end of the `<body>` tag
  
This follows the official Next.js App Router integration pattern for Speed Insights.

## Implementation Details:

The project uses Next.js 16.3.0 with the App Router architecture. The SpeedInsights component was added to the root layout file (`app/layout.tsx`) as recommended by Vercel's official documentation for Next.js App Router projects.

The component is placed at the end of the body tag, after the WorkspaceProvider, ensuring it doesn't interfere with the existing application structure while enabling automatic performance tracking.

## Verification:

✅ Build completed successfully (npm run build)
✅ All tests pass (17/17 tests passing)
✅ No new linting errors introduced
✅ Lock file updated correctly

## Notes:

- Speed Insights will automatically activate upon deployment to Vercel
- The tracking script is scoped at `/_vercel/speed-insights/*` routes
- No additional configuration is required for basic functionality
- The implementation is non-intrusive and preserves all existing functionality
